    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1946-10-10">October 10, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                    <salute>My dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                            Tillich</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4727" type="person">Mr. Trinterud</rs> has told me
                    that we are to have the benefit of your appraisal of <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__300" type="person">Dr. Emil Brunner</rs>&apos;s <rs
                        type="work" ref="#tillich__ASPVVH5A">REVELATION AND REASON</rs> for the
                    Westminster Bookman. This is indeed welcome news. Now I am wondering whether or
                    not it would be convenient for you to send us the review by <date
                        when="1946-10-21">October 21</date>, which has just been reported to me as
                    the copy due date for the next issue. We are looking forward with much interest
                    to the receipt of your article.<note type="ea"><rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Tillichs</rs> Rezension
                        erschien im Januar 1947. Vgl. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Paul Tillich</rs>: <rs type="work"
                            ref="#tillich__IVS4G69U">Emil Brunner: Revelation and Reason (1946)</rs>
                        (1947).</note></p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4726"
                            type="person">Ada Searon</rs><lb/>Assistant to the
                    Editors</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
